msgid "UI_HELP_BODY"
msgstr "This computer is a virtual terminal inside the game. Servers, sites, files and tools are all fictional; nothing reaches a real network, shell or web browser.\n\nWindows\n  Drag the title bar to move · double-click or □ to maximize/restore · drag the bottom-right corner to resize\n  ─ minimize · × close: hides the window only; sessions, input and history are kept\n  Ctrl/Cmd+1–9: Terminal · Mail · Browser · RequestLab · Tools · Files · Evidence · Case board · Status\n  Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+1–4: Terminals 1–4 · Ctrl/Cmd+Tab: switch window\n  F1 help · F6 taskbar · Shift+F6 top bar text size and pause · F10 back to studio\n  Esc outside a text field: pause\n\nTerminals\n  Terminals 1–4 share one world but each keeps its own connection, working directory, command history and password prompt.\n  Enter runs · ↑/↓ history · Tab completes · Esc clears input or cancels a password prompt · Ctrl+L or clear wipes the screen\n  Passwords are hidden and never recorded. exit and Disconnect close only that terminal's remote connection.\n\nBrowser and RequestLab\n  Only in-game virtual addresses open. The browser, curl and RequestLab share one virtual request handler.\n  RequestLab headers and body must be JSON objects; malformed input is not sent.\n\nTools\n  Tools are not answer buttons. Read the published observations, enter a hypothesis and compare results.\n  Empty input is never sent. Advanced JSON input is optional. Which tool you used never decides a case.\n\nCase board and hints\n  Shows the real status of the current goals. Hints open only when you ask, in order 1 → 2 → 3.\n  When every goal is met you can move to the next case. Switching cases keeps each case's state.\n\nSaving\n  Progress is saved automatically when the state changes. If saving fails, autosave pauses and you choose between restoring the backup or keeping damaged files and saving new.\n  Evidence pins, comparisons and notes are screen aids only; they are not saved or used to decide a case.\n\nAlerts\n  Alerts rise only for refused actions the server observed. Local typos, reading, switching windows and time passing never raise them."

